WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.740
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.870
Nestled high up in the peaks of the Himalayan
mountain range, in Northern India, just on

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:11.990
the border of Tibet, lies a mysterious lake
called Roopkund.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:17.300
Few have traveled to this remote body of water,
5,000 metres above sea level.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.989
But a deadly surprise awaits those who do
embark upon the long trek to visit this terrible

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.269
tarn.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:28.749
Bones, lots and lots of bones.

00:00:28.749 --> 00:00:35.020
Most of the year the lake is frozen over but
for one effervescent month each year the ice

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:40.890
melts, revealing the perilous scene at the
bottom of the murky water, for the lakebed

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.380
is littered with hundreds of skeletal human
remains.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.530
Human bones can also be found scattered around
the lake’s perimeter in alarming quantities.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:57.780
It has been estimated that there are skeletons
in and around Roopkund lake, of over 300 people.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:04.800
The skeletons were first discovered in the
19th century and they remained a morbid curiosity

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.350
for hundreds of years.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:13.210
But very few knew of their existence until
they were rediscovered during World War II,

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.689
in 1942.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:19.639
An investigation began, to discover where
the 300 people who perished at this remote

00:01:19.639 --> 00:01:25.359
mountain lake came from, and how they died.

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:29.999
The first and most obvious suspicion was that
they were the bodies of Japanese soldiers

00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:36.209
who were trying to sneak their way through
India, earlier on during the war, sneaky Japanese.

00:01:36.209 --> 00:01:39.770
And they died due to exposure to cold weather.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:46.079
But after further inspection it was deduced
that the skeletons were far too old to be

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:47.600
from the war.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:54.570
Disturbingly these skeletons weren’t just
bones, due to the dry and extremely cold air

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:59.609
they had been preserved for an astonishingly
long time.

00:01:59.609 --> 00:02:04.700
Upon the skeletons investigators found bits
of flesh, nails and hair.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:11.340
And like a scene from Lost, they also found
ancient wooden artifacts, leather shoes, iron

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:17.600
spearheads, wooden staves and jewelry and
an omnipotent man called Jacob, okay maybe

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.030
not that last bit.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:24.500
So surely these remains can’t be more than
a few decades old, otherwise the flesh would

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.160
have decayed long ago.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:33.940
Now this is where things get weird, okay things
are already pretty weird, but this next discovery

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.720
will blow your mind.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:42.470
Samples of the skeletons and surrounding artifacts
were taken to Oxford University where they

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:47.010
conducted radiocarbon dating to uncover their
age.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.510
The remains dated back to 850 AD.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.760
And they still had bits of flesh attached!

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.820
How come I have to chuck out food that starts
to look dodgy if it’s been in my freezer

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.380
for a couple of months, yet mother nature
can preserve parts of human bodies for almost

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.710
1,200 years?

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:11.540
No evidence of a settlement has ever been
found near the bodies, so it’s assumed all

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.420
300 people were travelling at the time of
their demise.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.610
So the obvious question is, what killed them
all?

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.910
Starvation, gangrene, a landslide, were they
attacked by marauders?

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.330
Was it aliens perhaps?

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:31.890
But before you’re so quick to blame aliens,
because I know you’re just dying to, perhaps

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.650
local legend can shed some light onto this.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.790
According to the legends, the once king of
Kannauj was traveling with his pregnant wife

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:47.010
on a pilgrimage, as part of the Nanda Devi
Raj Jat, which is a large pilgrimage that

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.270
takes place in these parts of India, every
12 years.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:57.040
Being wealthy, the king and his wife were
traveling with around 300 servants, among

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.980
them were his personal dance troupe.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:05.780
Because if you were traveling on a long pilgrimage
across the Himalayas you would obviously take

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.470
a dance troupe, in case you get bored or something,
and if you get stranded then you can always

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.640
eat them.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:19.420
However, the legend also tells of a freak
hailstorm around that time, when enormous

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:25.139
balls of ice pelted down from the sky, one
hit from such a mighty hailstone could quite

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:28.070
easily cause death.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:33.970
It could certainly wipe out a group of 300
pilgrims high up in the mountains, especially

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:40.540
when you consider that the lake is in a large
open expanse with little to no shelter nearby.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:47.370
In 2013 researchers examined the bodies in
more detail and discovered that every person

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:53.310
was killed by blows with a blunt object, to
the head, neck and shoulder region.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:58.541
The large, circular holes in the skeleton’s
skulls seems to suggest that the sudden and

00:04:58.541 --> 00:05:07.310
violent hailstorm legend could have been responsible
for the mysterious 9th century human remains.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:15.730
However, this theory is the best we have so
far, but the mystery has certainly not been

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:22.070
proven and there are many people who say the
hailstorm idea is completely wrong.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:27.970
The bodies all had damage to their heads and
shoulders but absolutely no damage below the

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.350
shoulders.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:34.210
Hailstones aren’t that selective, surely
if 300 people were killed by large balls of

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:40.040
ice, they would have sustained injuries all
over their bodies, some people would get knocked

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.800
over and pelted with hail on their torso and
legs.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.110
And what about their arms?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:50.610
People most certainly would have put their
arms above their heads in an attempt to protect

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.960
themselves.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.760
Yet no skeletons were found with injuries
to their arms.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.290
Hmm, suspicious.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:06.270
So then, until we come up with another, more
plausible solution to explain this most mysterious

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.330
conundrum, it will remain a mystery.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.230
I know, it was aliens, yep, definitely aliens.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:29.650
Thanks for watching.

